<title>UK: Lucas Varity seen entering FTSE 100.</title>
<headline>Lucas Varity seen entering FTSE 100.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in newly merged Anglo-U.S. autocomponents specialist Lucas Varity Plc are likely to be included in the FTSE 100 share index when the quarterly review committee meets on September 11, analysts said.</p>
<p>The listing of the newly formed company is expected to become effective on Friday at 1330 GMT, the Stock Exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>Prior to the merger Lucas Industries was in the FTSE Mid 250 index.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
